"""Vj_kc_v24_stranded_fix: Vj_kc_v23 with the _v234_rescue "already handled" bailout
fixed to require a nonzero WHEAT pickup quantity, not just a PICKUP,WHEAT
command shape. Root cause: when shed WHEAT hits 0 (more likely under our
retuned PET_CAFE margin, which tilts the agent harder toward CARROT), the
sheep-feeding worker (_v233_worker, 6-target compact variant) issues
['PICKUP','WHEAT',0] every turn forever (min(hungry, shed_wheat=0) = 0). The
existing _v234_rescue mechanism is SUPPOSED to catch exactly this shortage and
buy replacement WHEAT via the market, but its bailout check
`command[:2]==['PICKUP','WHEAT']` doesn't look at quantity, so a stuck
zero-quantity pickup is misread as "already handled" and rescue never fires.
Fix: only treat the pickup as handled when it requests a positive quantity.
"""
